= Decentralized identity — Simple =

Decentralized identity lets identifiers and verifiable claims be used without requiring one central identity provider for every interaction. It can use DIDs, credentials, keys, wallets, and other components, but none of those is the whole concept.

'''Important boundary:''' decentralized identity ≠ blockchain identity.

== Sources ==
* W3C, ''Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) v1.0'', Recommendation, 19 July 2022.
* W3C DID Core v1.1, Candidate Recommendation Snapshot, 5 March 2026, for ongoing standard evolution.
